#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096377 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4b340f6-0ac6-5bbf-a7d4-0088ca3c4e5e" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating the Exponential Function With a Linear Exponent"}] :question/id #uuid "9a42787b-24fb-50c8-9f3f-9e95d35c403c" :question/math-academy-id "e-459" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\displaystyle \\int e^{1-3x}\\, \\textrm{d}x}$." :question/worked-solution "If we let $u=1-3x$, then\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = -3\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm d x = -\\dfrac 1 3 \\textrm d u\n$$\n\nThen, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\inte^{1 - 3x}dx &= \\inte^{u} \\cdot (-\\frac{1}{3})du \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{3}\\inte^{u}du \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{3}e^{u} + C \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{3}e^{1 - 3x} + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096378 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "19fd901f-e08d-54c5-9cda-68543a3d71a9" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a General Exponential Function With a Linear Exponent"}] :question/id #uuid "cbf09123-3650-5d6a-869a-8edd8f54206b" :question/math-academy-id "e-460" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\displaystyle \\int 3^{5+4x}\\, \\textrm{d}x}$." :question/worked-solution "If we let\n\n$$\nu=5+4x\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = 4\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm d x = \\dfrac 1 4 \\textrm d u\n$$\n\nThen, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int3^{5 + 4x}dx &= \\int3^{u} \\cdot \\frac{1}{4}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4}\\int3^{u}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4} \\cdot \\frac{3^{u}}{\\ln 3} + C \\\\\n&= \\frac{3^{5 + 4x}}{4\\ln 3} + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
